{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"state","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Concurrent initialization can overwrite the persisted member identity, leaving one process with an identity that changes after restart."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Concurrent writes with distinct cancellation signals issue redundant API requests while both writes still succeed."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"test","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The required clock-skew coverage misses renewal and release cases, but the current implementation has no demonstrated clock-dependent runtime defect."}]}